### ⚠ ONE judge graded this

Two graders on this harness split on about **one item in three**, and
three readers scored the same candidate 2/6, 4/6 and 6/6 ordered by
nothing but leniency. A single judge's reading is a hypothesis about
this candidate, not a measurement of it, and nothing above can tell
you which items it would have read the other way.

Add a second and the items they disagree on stop being scored:

    CADRE_JUDGE='judge,<other-agent>' cadre grade candidate 2

Pick one whose failures you expect to differ from judge's. Two
graders of one lineage agree where one was already confident.


### What the score does not tell you

A hit rate ranks. It does not tell you whether this reviewer fails on the
SAME items your current panel already fails on. Compare the per-item rows
above against your incumbents': a lower-scoring candidate that hits an item
everyone else misses is worth more than a higher-scoring one that agrees
with them everywhere. See docs/METHOD.md.

